ue if you see requests being retracted frequently.'] = 1.0, page_size: Annotated[Optional[int], Arg(help='The number of tokens in a page.', choices=None, aliases=None, cli_name=None, type_parser=None, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=True, fallback=None)] = None, c128_page_size: Annotated[int, 'The physical page size of the NPU DSV4 C128 KV cache. Must be a positive multiple of 16.'] = 16, swa_full_tokens_ratio: Annotated[Optional[float], Arg(help='The ratio of SWA layer KV tokens / full layer KV tokens, regardless of the number of swa:full layers. It should be between 0 and 1. E.g. 0.5 means if each swa layer has 50 tokens, then each full layer has 100 tokens.', choices=None, aliases=None, cli_name=None, type_parser=None, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=True, fallback=0.8)] = None, disable_hybrid_swa_memory: Annotated[bool, Arg(help='Disable the hybrid SWA memory pool.', choices=None, aliases=None, cli_name=None, type_parser=None, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=True, fallback=None)] = False, radix_eviction_policy: Annotated[str, Arg(help="The eviction policy of radix trees. 'lru' stands for Least Recently Used, 'lfu' stands for Least Frequently Used, 'slru' stands for Segmented Least Recently Used, 'priority' evicts lower-priority requests first, and 'tlru' stands for Tail-Optimized LRU (arXiv:2510.15152), which evicts the part of a conversation that cannot affect tail TTFT before falling back to LRU. See https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/radix_eviction_policy for what each policy optimizes for.", choices=['lru', 'lfu', 'slru', 'priority', 'tlru'], aliases=None, cli_name=None, type_parser=None, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=True, fallback=None)] = 'lru', radix_eviction_policy_config: Annotated[Optional[Dict[str, Any]], Arg(help='Tuning parameters for --radix-eviction-policy, as a json object passed to the policy as keyword arguments. \'slru\' takes protected_threshold (int, default 2), e.g. \'{"protected_threshold": 4}\'; \'tlru\' takes threshold and next_prompt_estimate (ints, tokens), e.g. \'{"threshold": 4096, "next_prompt_estimate": 512}\'. An unrecognized key fails at startup, naming the key and the policy. See https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/radix_eviction_policy#policy-parameters for the full parameter list.', choices=None, aliases=None, cli_name=None, type_parser=<function loads at 0x7fbfd3fb6020>, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=False, fallback=None)] = None, prefill_only_disable_kv_cache: Annotated[bool, 'Skip the physical KV cache allocation for embedding-mode prefill-only workloads. Currently only valid with --is-embedding, --chunked-prefill-size=-1, --disable-radix-cache, an FA prefill backend, and non-FP4 KV cache so the fa_skip_kv_cache path is active (no layer reads or writes the cache). Other prefill-only workloads such as scoring/MIS may benefit from this later once their attention paths stop using paged KV. Scheduler admission accounting is unchanged; per-layer K/V tensors are sized to (page_size, head_num, head_dim) placeholders so GPU memory is not wasted.'] = False, disable_radix_cache: Annotated[bool, Arg(help='Disable RadixAttention for prefix caching.', choices=None, aliases=None, cli_name=None, type_parser=None, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=True, fallback=None)] = False, enable_page_major_kv_layout: Annotated[bool, "Store the Mamba state and full/SWA KV caches as one entry per token slot, holding every layer's state, in a single page-granular buffer instead of one buffer per layer. Implied by --enable-unified-memory, and currently supported only with it."] = False, enable_unified_memory: Annotated[bool, 'Replace the statically-partitioned hybrid-model pools (full-attn KV + SWA/Mamba state) with one byte buffer split dynamically between sub-pools. Requires stride-aware attention, linear-attention and Mamba backends; the allowed backends and the supported PD-disaggregation and speculative-decoding configurations are validated at startup.'] = False, disable_chunked_prefix_cache: Annotated[bool, 'Disable chunked prefix cache feature for deepseek, which should save overhead for short sequences.'] = False, disable_overlap_schedule: Annotated[bool, Arg(help='Disable the overlap scheduler, which overlaps the CPU scheduler with GPU model worker.', choices=None, aliases=None, cli_name=None, type_parser=None, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=True, fallback=None)] = False, num_continuous_decode_steps: Annotated[int, 'Run multiple continuous decoding steps to reduce scheduling overhead. This can potentially increase throughput but may also increase time-to-first-token latency. The default value is 1, meaning only run one decoding step at a time.'] = 1, scheduler_recv_interval: Annotated[int, 'The interval to poll requests in scheduler. Can be set to >1 to reduce the overhead of this.'] = 1, enable_mixed_chunk: Annotated[bool, 'Enabling mixing prefill and decode in a batch when using chunked prefill.'] = False, nccl_port: Annotated[Optional[int], 'The port for NCCL distributed environment setup. Defaults to a random port.'] = None, dist_timeout: Annotated[Optional[int], 'Set timeout for torch.distributed initialization.'] = None, dist_init_addr: Annotated[Optional[str], Arg(help='The host address for initializing distributed backend (e.g., `192.168.0.2:25000`).', choices=None, aliases=['--nccl-init-addr'], cli_name=None, type_parser=None, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=False, fallback=None)] = None, gated_launch_port: Annotated[Optional[int], 'The port of the gated launch control server. When set, every rank blocks right after the distributed environment is initialized, before any sizable GPU allocation, until `POST /gate/activate` is sent to this port on the host of the first rank. This lets an external orchestrator defer the memory hungry part of startup to a safe window. Defaults to None, which disables the gate.'] = None, nnodes: Annotated[int, 'The number of nodes.'] = 1, node_rank: Annotated[int, 'The node rank.'] = 0, tp_size: Annotated[int, Arg(help='The tensor parallelism size.', choices=None, aliases=['--tensor-parallel-size'], cli_name=None, type_parser=None, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=False, fallback=None)] = 1, dcp_size: Annotated[int, Arg(help='The decode context parallelism size.', choices=None, aliases=['--decode-context-parallel-size'], cli_name=None, type_parser=None, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=False, fallback=None)] = 1, pp_size: Annotated[int, Arg(help='The pipeline parallelism size.', choices=None, aliases=['--pipeline-parallel-size'], cli_name=None, type_parser=None, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=False, fallback=None)] = 1, pp_max_micro_batch_size: Annotated[Optional[int], 'The maximum micro batch size in pipeline parallelism.'] = None, pp_async_batch_depth: Annotated[int, 'The async batch depth of pipeline parallelism.'] = 0, dp_size: Annotated[int, Arg(help='The number of data-parallel replicas of the model.', choices=None, aliases=['--data-parallel-size'], cli_name=None, type_parser=None, nargs=None, required=None, action=None, action_kwargs=None, const=None, no_cli=False, resolvable=True, fallback=None)] = 1, attn_dp_size: Annotated[int, Arg(help='The attention data parallelism size: the number of data-parallel attention groups inside the TP group, one scheduler each